WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.513
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Advanced.

2
00:00:05.813 --> 00:00:09.246
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.546 --> 00:00:17.829
Unit twenty-eight: Sports and Ethics. In this unit, you will discuss fairness and money in modern sport.

4
00:00:18.817 --> 00:00:20.352
performance enhancement.

5
00:00:21.052 --> 00:00:26.732
performance enhancement means improving athletic results, sometimes through banned methods.

6
00:00:27.032 --> 00:00:29.705
Performance enhancement through drugs is banned.

7
00:00:30.405 --> 00:00:33.916
Your turn. Say: performance enhancement.

8
00:00:36.616 --> 00:00:38.256
performance enhancement.

9
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:40.356
gene doping.

10
00:00:41.056 --> 00:00:45.842
gene doping means illegally changing genes to improve athletic ability.

11
00:00:46.142 --> 00:00:49.581
Gene doping could become sport's next big scandal.

12
00:00:50.281 --> 00:00:53.374
Your turn. Say: gene doping.

13
00:00:56.074 --> 00:00:57.296
gene doping.

14
00:00:58.283 --> 00:00:59.644
sportswashing.

15
00:01:00.344 --> 00:01:05.467
sportswashing means using sport to improve a country's or company's damaged reputation.

16
00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:08.254
Critics accused the hosts of sportswashing.

17
00:01:08.954 --> 00:01:12.408
Your turn. Say: sportswashing.

18
00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:16.445
sportswashing.

19
00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:18.939
athlete welfare.

20
00:01:19.639 --> 00:01:25.040
athlete welfare means the health, safety and wellbeing of athletes.

21
00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:27.978
Athlete welfare must come before medals.

22
00:01:28.678 --> 00:01:32.073
Your turn. Say: athlete welfare.

23
00:01:34.773 --> 00:01:36.413
athlete welfare.

24
00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:39.010
concussion protocol.

25
00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:45.355
concussion protocol means official rules for treating head injuries in sport.

26
00:01:45.655 --> 00:01:48.618
The player was removed under the concussion protocol.

27
00:01:49.318 --> 00:01:53.027
Your turn. Say: concussion protocol.

28
00:01:55.727 --> 00:01:57.239
concussion protocol.

29
00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.041
commercialisation of sport.

30
00:02:00.741 --> 00:02:06.119
commercialisation of sport means the growing influence of money and business in sport.

31
00:02:06.419 --> 00:02:09.904
The commercialisation of sport has raised ticket prices.

32
00:02:10.604 --> 00:02:14.104
Your turn. Say: commercialisation of sport.

33
00:02:16.804 --> 00:02:18.769
commercialisation of sport.

34
00:02:19.783 --> 00:02:20.889
amateurism.

35
00:02:21.589 --> 00:02:25.400
amateurism means doing sport for love, not money.

36
00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.744
The Olympics once required strict amateurism.

37
00:02:29.444 --> 00:02:32.584
Your turn. Say: amateurism.

38
00:02:35.284 --> 00:02:36.413
amateurism.

39
00:02:37.417 --> 00:02:38.836
integrity unit.

40
00:02:39.536 --> 00:02:44.287
integrity unit means an organisation that investigates cheating in sport.

41
00:02:44.587 --> 00:02:47.446
Tennis has an independent integrity unit.

42
00:02:48.146 --> 00:02:51.785
Your turn. Say: integrity unit.

43
00:02:54.485 --> 00:02:55.927
integrity unit.

44
00:02:56.917 --> 00:02:59.067
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:03.851
Ms. Sarah, should athletes be allowed to use any performance enhancement?

46
00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:09.669
Most experts insist that drugs be banned, mainly for athlete welfare.

47
00:03:10.983 --> 00:03:13.285
But what about gene doping in the future?

48
00:03:14.583 --> 00:03:19.242
It is essential that regulators prepare now, before it becomes possible.

49
00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.770
And head injuries? Some players return far too soon.

50
00:03:26.083 --> 00:03:30.730
Doctors recommend that every league follow a strict concussion protocol.

51
00:03:32.017 --> 00:03:34.527
Money seems to dominate everything now.

52
00:03:35.817 --> 00:03:41.104
Yes. Were it not for commercialisation, sportswashing would be far less tempting.

53
00:03:42.417 --> 00:03:46.680
Grammar focus: Subjunctive and formal structures (extended).

54
00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:51.267
The subjunctive is common in formal rules and recommendations.

55
00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:56.901
Experts insist that drugs be banned. It is crucial that every league follow the protocol.

56
00:03:57.201 --> 00:03:59.862
Were it not for money, sport would be different.

57
00:04:00.162 --> 00:04:05.181
The subjunctive is typical of rules, policies and formal recommendations.

58
00:04:06.183 --> 00:04:09.196
Now read and listen. Winning at What Cost?.

59
00:04:09.496 --> 00:04:14.699
Modern sport is a global industry worth hundreds of billions of dollars.

60
00:04:15.983 --> 00:04:21.280
The commercialisation of sport has brought professionalism, but also new ethical problems.

61
00:04:22.583 --> 00:04:27.369
Doping scandals have damaged trust in cycling, athletics and other sports.

62
00:04:28.683 --> 00:04:32.599
Scientists warn that gene doping may soon be difficult to detect.

63
00:04:33.883 --> 00:04:38.553
At the same time, concussion research has forced leagues to rethink player safety.

64
00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:44.183
Some countries have been accused of sportswashing by hosting major tournaments.

65
00:04:45.483 --> 00:04:50.176
Independent integrity units now investigate corruption and match-fixing.

66
00:04:51.483 --> 00:04:55.317
It is essential that the spirit of fair play survive the pressure of money.

67
00:04:56.617 --> 00:04:59.942
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:05:00.242 --> 00:05:03.844
Using sport to improve a damaged reputation is blank.

69
00:05:04.144 --> 00:05:10.096
A, amateurism. B, sportswashing. C, athlete welfare.

70
00:05:14.083 --> 00:05:16.896
The answer is B: sportswashing.

71
00:05:18.383 --> 00:05:21.474
The coach insisted that every player blank on time.

72
00:05:21.774 --> 00:05:25.474
A, arrives. B, arrive. C, arrived.

73
00:05:29.483 --> 00:05:31.460
The answer is B: arrive.

74
00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:35.333
It is essential that she blank informed.

75
00:05:35.633 --> 00:05:38.694
A, be. B, is. C, was.

76
00:05:42.683 --> 00:05:44.358
The answer is A: be.

77
00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:48.755
Official rules for treating head injuries are a blank.

78
00:05:49.055 --> 00:05:55.309
A, concussion protocol. B, integrity unit. C, gene doping.

79
00:05:59.317 --> 00:06:02.895
The answer is A: concussion protocol.

80
00:06:04.383 --> 00:06:08.275
According to the text, what may soon be difficult to detect?

81
00:06:08.575 --> 00:06:13.587
A, match-fixing. B, gene doping. C, injuries.

82
00:06:17.583 --> 00:06:19.989
The answer is B: gene doping.

83
00:06:21.483 --> 00:06:26.365
Now it's your turn. Part one: Has money damaged the spirit of sport?

84
00:06:31.665 --> 00:06:38.169
Part two: Use the subjunctive in a recommendation, give two arguments and one example.

85
00:06:44.469 --> 00:06:59.004
To some extent, yes. High salaries create pressure to cheat, and sportswashing exploits fans. I would recommend that every federation publish its finances. Cycling's doping scandals show what happens when money outweighs ethics.

86
00:06:59.304 --> 00:07:01.977
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:07:02.983 --> 00:07:08.689
Great work today! You learned eight new words and subjunctive and formal structures (extended).

88
00:07:08.989 --> 00:07:13.255
Today's value is fair play. Play fairly and follow the rules.

89
00:07:13.555 --> 00:07:17.728
See you in Unit twenty-nine. Goodbye!

90
00:07:18.028 --> 00:07:20.750
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

